  "cil_liability": true,
  "street_name": "Gander Green Lane",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would result in the conversion of a single family residential dwelling where the Gross Internal Area of the original dwelling is less than 125sqm and it is located outside of an Area of Potential Intensification. The proposal would therefore result in the overdevelopment of the site, loss of family housing without the provision of better-designed or higher-quality housing, contrary to Policy 10 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018. As such the proposed development is considered to be unacceptable in principle.",
    "The development, by reasons of the site layout on a constrained site appears as an incompatible and incongruous addition to the wider surrounding area resulting in a cramped and overly developed site with excessive subdivision, hard standing and off street parking. As such, the proposal fails to respect the context of the housing in this area and has a significant harmful effect on the appearance of the surrounding area contrary to the principles of the National Planning Policy Framework, policy D3 and D4  of the London Plan, policies 1 and 28 of the Sutton Local Plan and SPD 14 Creating Locally Distinctive Places.",
    "Without evidence to the contrary, the application has failed to demonstrate that the proposal will provide a satisfactorily reduction in carbon emissions and that internal potable water consumption for each of the dwellings will be limited to 110 litres per person per day. As such, the application would be contrary to Policy SI 2 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy 31 and 33 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The proposed location of the two off-street parking spaces accessed off Gander Green Lane would result in a highway safety concern given the proximity to the road junction between Gander Green Lane and Brocks Drive. As such the proposal is contrary to Policy T4 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy 36 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "By reason of the insufficient size of three of the outdoor amenity spaces proposed and the proposed front garden car parking arrangement, the proposal would result in an unacceptable impact on the future occupiers of the development contrary to Policy 9 and 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018."
  ],
